ices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Lengthen the answer with adjectives while keeping the same idea","Locate precise textual evidence, then explain how language choices shape meaning or effect","Guess from the title alone with no textual clue","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged"],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to analyse false friend and explain why it matters?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake","Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess","Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length"],"question":"Which revision actually improves meaning for gloss?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Accurate transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change fonts and claim the work is new","Skipping glosses and bluffing","Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about gloss","Retype the worked model as the final answer"],"question":"Which response shows accurate use of gloss on fresh material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about gloss with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating gloss on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using gloss on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful